Dear ALSA folks,


running Debian Wheezy with Linux 3.2.23 on a T60 with

         0 [Intel          ]: HDA-Intel - HDA Intel
                              HDA Intel at 0xee240000 irq 46
        29 [ThinkPadEC     ]: ThinkPad EC - ThinkPad Console Audio Control
                              ThinkPad Console Audio Control at EC reg 0x30=
, fw 79HT50WW-1.07

(attached `alsa-info.sh` output from before running the following
command) despite enabling power saving

        $ echo 1 | sudo tee /sys/module/snd_hda_intel/parameters/power_save
        1

and touching the device or playing some music, I am able to hear a
pop/click before playing another piece of music, so some power saving
mode seems to be enabled, Powertop 2.1 built from Git still shows the
device using 100 %.

Others seem to have similar problem with other devices though [1].


Thanks,

Paul


[1] http://mancoosi.org/~abate/audio-codec-hwc0d0-conexant-and-powertop

